{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128374-enchanting-wonders-group-approach","id":1128374,"title":"Enchanting Wonders - Group Approach","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-13T02:43:36-07:00","id":1128374,"title":"Enchanting Wonders - Group Approach","content":"I have some questions about the crafting of Wonders. In the group that I ST, I've got a Prime focussed character (Ex-Templar CC) who is slanted towards the creation and enchantment of items. Currently, the PCs are dealing with some Kindred - and have had the idea to create some trinkets that provide Mind Shield (to help with that pesky Obfuscate). The CC character has Prime 3/Matter 2/ Forces 2, but no Mind 1. I'm considering allowing them to work as a group, creating the trinkets together in their shared Node/Sanctum (for which they all put in points for). <br /> <br /> 1) In The Book of Secrets (and Core M20), it indicates that you need to have the Spheres necessary for the effect to be invested into the Wonder being created. My reading is that the person doing the enchantment (i.e. the CC) needs to have the appropriate Sphere (Mind 1). Would you allow a Cabal to work in concert, instead? I'm happy to do it if they've got good story reasons and explanations for doing so. In this way, the CC would be the keystone of the ritual, but the CoE in the Cabal would provide the Mind expertise.<br /> <br /> 2) The SoE in their Cabal has the Hands of Daedalus Merit. Similarly to the question asked above in (1), would you allow them to assist/take the lead in the physical crafting of the object?<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm really asking is whether the various tasks involved in Wonder creation can be split up amongst Cabal members. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T08:11:54-07:00","id":1128441,"title":"","content":"Various tasks yes. The enchanter doesn't need to be the objects crafter. Though the objects to be enchanted need to fit the paradigm of the enchanter. A Verbena wouldn't be able to create a laser weapon crafted by a SoE.<br /> <br /> The enchantment process can be shared as well as long as those involved are on the same standing as to how magick works. This is described in the section detailing Rituals in M20. As creating a Wonder is simply an extended ritual at it's core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:03:32-07:00","id":1128587,"title":"","content":"Oh, thanks for your input! I didn't see that shown in the rituals section. (Admittedly, I've not read the entirety of the almost-700 page core book, so appreciate you highlighting this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T14:17:29-07:00","id":1128959,"title":"","content":"You can certainly allow it, since you are the ST.<br /> <br /> RAW the one leading the ritual has to have all necessary sphere levels, the assistants add 1 success if they have all the necessary spheres but not the required dots, co-workers add their full Arete but need all necessary sphere levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T02:19:38-07:00","id":1129719,"title":"","content":"I would allow it if the CC in this case had Mind 1. Which in this particular case makes it unnecessary for the other to participate.<br /> Take the example that 3 mages want to create a Talisman that has a Forces 3, Matter 3 and Correspondence 3 effect along with Prime 4 to fuel it..<br /> Mage 1 has Prime 4, Matter 3 and Forces and Correspondence at 1.<br /> Mage 2 has Forces 3 but the others at 1.<br /> Mage 3 had Correspondence at 3 and the others at 1.<br /> <br /> The one with Prime 4 &quot;leads&quot; the creation and can direct the other two mages in the process and the others can contribute their expertise.<br /> <br /> If one or more of the mages did not possess the necessary Spheres at at least 1 or if the sum total of the 3 mages sphere levels did not match the necessary levels of Prime 4, Forces 3, Matter 3 and Correspondence 3 the creation of the item wouldn't work. It's the same rules i use for collaborative casting in rituals.<br /> <br /> Hope that i make sense in what i'm trying to say here.<br /> <br /> Edit: And of course, all the characters paradigms needs to be at least compatible. Preferably the characters should be of the same tradition/convention/craft/whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":392,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","user":"Cadmiumcadamium","date":". 08-16-2017, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}